              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Christina"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was good! I've never used canned yams, so I wasn't sure what to expect, but they worked well in this. Also, I couldn't find regular canned apples, but I did find 'fried' cinnamon apples in syrup, so I used those and that was great. I think next time I will use less (if any) of the canned syrups and maybe use some maple syrup instead b/c I was hoping that it woiuld be a bit sweeter. All in all, this was a nice, quick side and everyone at the dinner table enjoyed it (including my sweet potato hating hubby, lol). I will def be making this again! Thanks for sharing. :)",
            "datePublished": "2012-11-08T17:57:29.610Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Elaine Wilson"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is very good. I don't care for yams but this recipe is not over sugared. I use this for potlucks and everyone loves it. The only thing I change is I drain the yams. Its too much liquid and makes it hard to transport. Reserve the yam liquid until you see how moist its going to be. I use apple pie filling for the sliced apples.",
            "datePublished": "2012-01-10T16:07:08.207Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
